  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Use lean beef or horse meat. Remove fat and connective tissue before grinding. Mix meat, water and NaOH, then boil for 15 min with stirring. Cool toroom temperature, skim fat off surface, and filter, retaining both meat particles and filtrate. To the filtrate add water to a final volumeof 1000 ml, and then add:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "To make medium anoxic boil it, cool under 100% N2 gas atmosphere, add 0.5 g/l L-cysteine hydrochloride and adjust pH to 7.0.Dispense under same gas atmosphere 7 ml medium into Hungate-type tubes (for strains demanding meat particles put those first into the tube (use 1 part meat particles to 4 or 5 parts fluid)). Autoclave at 121°C for 30 min. For agar slants use 15.0 g agar per 1000.0 ml medium."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "In some cases (as indicated in the catalogue) the addition of Haemin and Vitamin K1 or Vitamin K3 is necessary. Add to 1000.0 ml of medium after autoclaving:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "Dissolve 50 mg haemin in 1 ml 1 N NaOH; make up to 100 ml withdistilled water and filter sterilize. Store refrigerated."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 15,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": "Dissolve 0.1 ml of vitamin K1 in 20 ml 95% ethanol and filter sterilize. Store refrigerated in a brown bottle."
    }
  ]
}